{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{"tools":{"listChanged":false}},"serverInfo":{"name":"pgmemu","version":"devel"},"instructions":"PGMEmu emulates the IGS PolyGame Master arcade board. Load a game with emu_load_game (a set name such as orlegend; pgm is the BIOS alone), run it with emu_run_frames (60 frames is about a second) or emu_run_until, and look at it with video_screenshot, video_sprites, memory_read and cpu_get_state (cpu m68k, z80 or arm7). Runs stop early at breakpoints (debug_breakpoint_add, on any of the three CPUs) and watchpoints (debug_watchpoint_add); debug_trace shows the last 68000 instructions. input_press presses a button for a moment, input_set holds it; memory_write changes RAM; state_save and state_load keep and restore a moment. Integers may be written as hex strings, \"0x1000\". Time is counted in master ticks of 50 MHz. The tools are the methods of docs/spec/control-protocol.md."}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"audio_capture_start","description":"Starts recording the sound to a WAV file at the ICS2115's own rate, about 33 kHz; runs add to it as they end.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the WAV."}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"audio_capture_stop","description":"Ends the sound recording and completes the WAV file.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"audio_voices","description":"The ICS2115's active voices and their registers.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"cpu_disassemble","description":"Disassembles 68000 or ARM7 instructions from an address.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"Where to start."},"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many instructions, at most 1000."},"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k (the default) or arm7."},"thumb":{"type":"boolean","description":"ARM7: Thumb rather than ARM instructions; the ARM7's own state if left out."}},"required":["address","count"]}},{"name":"cpu_get_state","description":"A CPU's registers: the 68000's or the IGS027A's ARM7, with the instruction at its PC, or the Z80's.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k (the default), z80 or arm7."}}}},{"name":"debug_breakpoint_add","description":"Stops runs where a processor executes the instruction at an address: the 68000 before it executes it.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The instruction's address."},"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k (the default), z80 or arm7 (the IGS027A's). A Z80 or ARM7 breakpoint stops the run after the 68000 instruction during which that processor reached it; the processor itself has run on."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_breakpoint_list","description":"The addresses of a processor's breakpoints, ascending.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k (the default), z80 or arm7."}}}},{"name":"debug_breakpoint_remove","description":"Removes a breakpoint.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The breakpoint's address."},"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k (the default), z80 or arm7."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_trace","description":"The last instructions the 68000 executed, oldest first, with when each began in master ticks.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many, at most 4096; 32 if left out."}}}},{"name":"debug_watchpoint_add","description":"Stops runs after a 68000 instruction that reads or writes data in a range of addresses. Instruction fetches do not count.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The range's first address."},"size":{"type":"integer","description":"Bytes in the range; 1 if left out."},"access":{"type":"string","description":"read, write (the default) or access, for both."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_watchpoint_list","description":"The watchpoints.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"debug_watchpoint_remove","description":"Removes the watchpoint at an address.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The watchpoint's first address."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_link_read","description":"Receives bytes the test ROM sent over the debug link, running the machine until at least min_bytes have come or the timeout passes. available is what is left to read.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"max_bytes":{"type":"integer","description":"The most bytes to answer."},"min_bytes":{"type":"integer","description":"The fewest to wait for; 0 if left out."},"timeout_cycles":{"type":"integer","description":"Master ticks to wait at most; 2000000 if left out."}},"required":["max_bytes"]}},{"name":"debug_link_start","description":"Opens PGMTest's debug link, as the simulator does: through the RFIF block the test ROM publishes in work RAM. comms_addr, the ROM mailbox's address, is taken and not used.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"debug_link_stop","description":"Closes the debug link, telling the test ROM so.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"debug_link_write","description":"Sends bytes to the test ROM over the debug link, running the machine until the test ROM has published its block and the bytes fit in its ring.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"data_hex":{"type":"string","description":"The bytes, as hex."},"timeout_cycles_per_byte":{"type":"integer","description":"Master ticks to give up after, per byte; 2000000 if left out."}},"required":["data_hex"]}},{"name":"emu_cartridge_info","description":"What the loaded cartridge image holds: names, hardware class, and each ROM with its type, size, mapping and CRC32.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_load_game","description":"Loads a game, powering a new board up: by set name from the ROM directory (pgm for the BIOS alone), or by path to a .pgm file. Give one of the two.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"A set name, such as orlegend; pgm loads the BIOS alone."},"path":{"type":"string","description":"The path of a .pgm file."},"region":{"type":"string","description":"The region the game runs as: one of the codes emu.cartridge_info lists, such as WRLD or JAPN. Without it the game runs as its image holds."}}}},{"name":"emu_pause","description":"Pauses the game where it runs by itself: in the desktop application, which then runs it only on request. A breakpoint or a watchpoint its own run reaches pauses it too. pgmemu-cli runs only on request anyway.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_reset","description":"Holds the board's reset line for some master ticks, the raster running on, then lets it go.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"cycles":{"type":"integer","description":"Master ticks (50 MHz) to hold reset for; 100 is what the RTL simulator's front end uses."}},"required":["cycles"]}},{"name":"emu_resume","description":"Lets the game run by itself again, where it does: in the desktop application.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_run_cycles","description":"Runs for at least some master ticks (50 MHz), stopping between 68000 instructions. Stops early at a breakpoint or a watchpoint.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Master ticks to run."}},"required":["count"]}},{"name":"emu_run_frames","description":"Runs until some frame boundaries have passed, where vblank begins. Stops early at a breakpoint or a watchpoint; the answer then says which.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Frames to run; 60 is about a second."}},"required":["count"]}},{"name":"emu_run_until","description":"Runs until a condition holds after a 68000 instruction, or a timeout passes. Conditions: {type: cpu_pc_equals, value}, {type: cpu_pc_in_range | cpu_pc_out_of_range, start, end}, {type: signal_equals | signal_not_equals | signal_less_than | signal_less_equal | signal_greater_than | signal_greater_equal, signal: vblank | hblank | line | frame, value}, and {type: and | or | not, children: [...]}.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"condition":{"type":"object","description":"The condition, as described above."},"timeout_cycles":{"type":"integer","description":"Master ticks to give up after; about 20 s of emulated time if left out."}},"required":["condition"]}},{"name":"emu_set_bios","description":"Where the BIOS files are taken from for the loads that follow: directories and zips, the first that has a file winning. The game loaded runs on undisturbed.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"sources":{"type":"array","description":"Paths of directories or zips, such as the path of pgm.zip."}},"required":["sources"]}},{"name":"emu_set_region","description":"Powers the board up again with the loaded game made another region, as loading it with that region would.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"region":{"type":"string","description":"One of the codes emu.cartridge_info lists, such as WRLD or JAPN."}},"required":["region"]}},{"name":"emu_status","description":"The emulator's version, the loaded game, the region it runs as, the emulated time (master ticks of 50 MHz and frames since power-up), whether the window's own run is paused, and the breakpoint or watchpoint the last run stopped at.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"input_clear","description":"Lets a control of player 1 go.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"up, down, left, right, button1 to button4, start or coin."}},"required":["name"]}},{"name":"input_get_state","description":"The controls held, in the RTL simulator's encoding.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"input_press","description":"Presses a control of player 1 for two frames and releases it for two: four frames run.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"up, down, left, right, button1 to button4, start or coin."}},"required":["name"]}},{"name":"input_set","description":"Holds a control of player 1 down until input.clear.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"up, down, left, right, button1 to button4, start or coin."}},"required":["name"]}},{"name":"memory_list_regions","description":"The names of the memory regions memory.read can read now.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"memory_read","description":"Reads bytes of a memory region, at most 1 MB, answered as lowercase hex. Work RAM is in 68000 byte order: the high byte of a word first.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"region":{"type":"string","description":"A name from memory.list_regions, such as WORK_RAM, VIDEO_RAM, PALETTE_RAM or AUDIO_RAM."},"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The first byte's offset in the region."},"size":{"type":"integer","description":"How many bytes, at most 1048576."}},"required":["region","address","size"]}},{"name":"memory_write","description":"Writes bytes into a RAM, as a debugger does: no bus cycle is made. The bytes are laid out as memory.read reads them; work RAM in 68000 byte order. The whole range is checked first, so the write is made whole or not at all.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"region":{"type":"string","description":"WORK_RAM, VIDEO_RAM, PALETTE_RAM or AUDIO_RAM. The ROMs cannot be written."},"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The first byte's offset in the region."},"data_hex":{"type":"string","description":"The bytes, two hex digits each."}},"required":["region","address","data_hex"]}},{"name":"nvram_load","description":"Loads the work RAM from a file nvram.save wrote.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"filename":{"type":"string","description":"A file name in the state directory, or a path."}},"required":["filename"]}},{"name":"nvram_save","description":"Saves the battery-backed work RAM, 128 KB, as the RTL's NVRAM interface lays it out: each word's low byte first.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"filename":{"type":"string","description":"A file name in the state directory, or a path."}},"required":["filename"]}},{"name":"state_list","description":"The save states in the state directory.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"state_load","description":"Restores a state that state.save wrote from the game now loaded.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"filename":{"type":"string","description":"A file name in the state directory, or a path."}},"required":["filename"]}},{"name":"state_save","description":"Saves the whole machine's state to a file, to be loaded later into the same game.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"filename":{"type":"string","description":"A file name in the state directory, or a path."}},"required":["filename"]}},{"name":"test_status","description":"The status block PGMTest's pages publish at the top of work RAM, 0x81F000: a 16-bit magic naming the page, then words whose meaning is the page's own.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"words":{"type":"integer","description":"How many 16-bit words to answer, magic included; 32 if left out."}}}},{"name":"video_layers","description":"Which layers the picture is drawn with, to see what lies under one; sets those given, answers all three. Drawn pictures and screenshots follow it from the next line.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"boolean","description":"The text layer."},"background":{"type":"boolean","description":"The background."},"sprites":{"type":"boolean","description":"The sprites."}}}},{"name":"video_registers","description":"IGS023's 16 registers and its zoom table, with the scroll registers named.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"video_screenshot","description":"The last complete picture, 448 by 224, as a PNG: written to a path, or returned in the answer.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the PNG; left out, the PNG is returned."}}}},{"name":"video_sprites","description":"The sprites of the list sprite DMA last copied from work RAM, which the picture shows from the next vertical blank, in list order: a later one draws over an earlier one.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"video_tilemap","description":"A layer's whole tile map as an image, unscrolled: the text layer's 64 by 32 tiles (512 by 256), the background's 64 by 16 (2048 by 512), which is all its 4 KB of VRAM holds. Transparent pixels are dark grey.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"layer":{"type":"string","description":"text or background."},"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the image as a PNG; left out, it is returned."},"format":{"type":"string","description":"png (the default), or rgba for raw pixels in rgba_base64."}},"required":["layer"]}},{"name":"video_tiles","description":"Tiles of the text layer (8 by 8) or the background (32 by 32) as an image, from the tile ROMs, in one of the layer's 32 palette groups. Transparent pixels are dark grey.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"layer":{"type":"string","description":"text or background."},"first":{"type":"integer","description":"The first tile code; 0 if left out."},"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many tiles, at most 4096; 256 if left out."},"columns":{"type":"integer","description":"Tiles to a row; 16 if left out."},"palette":{"type":"integer","description":"The palette group, 0 to 31; 0 if left out."},"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the image as a PNG; left out, it is returned."},"format":{"type":"string","description":"png (the default), or rgba for raw pixels in rgba_base64."}},"required":["layer"]}}]}}
