{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":12,"result":{"protocolVersion":"2025-11-25","capabilities":{"tools":{"listChanged":false}},"serverInfo":{"name":"pgmemu","version":"devel"},"instructions":"PGMEmu emulates the IGS PolyGame Master arcade board. Load a game with emu_load_game (a set name such as orlegend; pgm is the BIOS alone), run it with emu_run_frames (60 frames is about a second) or emu_run_until, and look at it with video_screenshot, video_sprites, memory_read and cpu_get_state (cpu m68k, z80 or arm7). Runs stop early at breakpoints (debug_breakpoint_add, on any of the three CPUs) and watchpoints (debug_watchpoint_add); debug_trace shows the last 68000 instructions. input_press presses a button for a moment, input_set holds it; memory_write changes RAM; state_save and state_load keep and restore a moment. Integers may be written as hex strings, \"0x1000\". Time is counted in master ticks of 50 MHz. The tools are the methods of docs/spec/control-protocol.md."}}
